  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - EARTHQUAKE AFTERSHOCK PREDICTION AND LANDSLIDE MONITORING, through U.S. Government - Department of Interior</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA funding of a $198,330 supports technical assistance (TA) to help China improve its ability to accurately predict and monitor earthquake aftershocks and landslides. This TA focuses on Sichuan Province, the area most impacted by the May 2008 earthquake, and entails a two-year training program for officials from the China Earthquake Administration (CEA) and the China Geological Survey (CGS). A team of research seismologists led by the U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) conducts this training, which also involves installation of pilot aftershock and landslide monitoring systems and operational training on their use.</narrative>
  </description>
